AB  - 3D vision-language models are vulnerable to adversarial point-cloud attacks despite their strong zero-shot generalization capabilities, and test-time defenses for CLIP-based models do not fully transfer to the 3D regime. This letter proposes TRDefense, a training-free test-time defense method for 3D vision-language models. TRDefense applies a set of compound point-cloud transformations to probe the visual encoder and uses the induced feature changes to estimate a correction direction for feature repair, with a point-dropping response-consistency score used to select the repair strength. This design exploits our observation that compound point-cloud transformations induce stable repair directions, whereas point-dropping responses provide a more reliable cue for distinguishing clean-like and adversarial-like inputs. Experiments across multiple datasets and models show that TRDefense improves adversarial accuracy while largely preserving clean accuracy and provides complementary robustness gains on adversarially trained models.
