KW  - Vulnerability detection
KW  - In-context learning
KW  - Chain of thought
KW  - Smart contract
KW  - Blockchain
AB  - Blockchain technology has seen widespread adoption across various sectors, making the security of smart contracts essential for the reliable operation of blockchain networks. Conventional static detection tools often fall short, suffering from false negatives due to limited semantic analysis and dependence on predefined rules. In contrast, deep learning-based methods offer superior performance by continuously updating their knowledge base and learning the nuanced characteristics of potential vulnerabilities. This paper presents SmartGuard, an enhanced framework for smart contract vulnerability detection that leverages Large Language Models (LLMs). SmartGuard identifies vulnerabilities by retrieving semantically similar code snippets, generating corresponding Chains of Thought (CoT), and combining these elements for in-context learning. To optimize the use of labeled data for automatic CoT generation, we introduce a self-check architecture that utilizes the self-correcting capabilities of LLMs to produce high-quality reasoning chains. Evaluations on the SolidiFI benchmark dataset demonstrate a recall of 95.06% and an F1-score of 94.95%, outperforming existing tools. Further experiments across multiple models confirm the framework’s generalizability. The code is publicly available at https://github.com/KevinClaint/SmartGuard.
